<title>RUSSIA: Russian Jan-August GDP falls six pct.</title>
<headline>Russian Jan-August GDP falls six pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gross domestic product in the first eight months of this year totalled 1,403 trillion roubles, which was six percent less than a year earlier in inflation-adjusted terms, the State Statistics Committee said on Friday.</p>
<p>GDP in August was eight percent lower than a year earlier.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			  AUG 96    JUL 96    AUG 95</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	  +5	  +1	  +4</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	    -8	  -9	  -4</p>
<p>Note - Official Russian data tend to underreport a growing private sector in the economy.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
